  clock: 4  # e76e
  nonce: e76e  # e76e
  message: "SATISFIED by PR #312, merged as c4e193314e, against the statement as filed —\n\"A confirmed verdict must disclose whether it relied on user-supplied catalogue\ninput.\" Behavioural evidence re-run on the MERGED tree, with its negative\ncontrol:\n\n  verify-claims selfgrade --claims selfgrade/claims.yaml     -> rc 0, and now:\n    NOTE: these verdicts were computed against USER-SUPPLIED catalogue input.\n      io_primitives: selfgrade/hypergumbo-overlay.yaml  [claims-file extra_catalogs]\n      ... Where a claims-file catalogue ships inside the analysed repo, the\n      repository is supplying its own criteria (INV-zosun).\n\n  CONTROL, shipped catalogue only (the INV-buzab telnet fixture):\n    text disclosure renders to NOTHING; --json catalog_provenance.user_supplied\n    is False. So the signal is not always-on decoration.\n\nBOTH SURFACES. `catalog_provenance` in the --json envelope\n(VERIFY_CLAIMS_SCHEMA_VERSION 1.8 -> 1.9), always present so `user_supplied:\nfalse` is assertable rather than an absent key, plus the text renderer — a\ndisclosure that exists only under --json is half shipped (INV-karud a3's\nprecedent). The pre-existing stderr line was weaker than json-only: any\nredirect discards it and it was not attached to the verdict.\n\nTHE CLI AND CLAIMS-FILE LAYERS ARE REPORTED SEPARATELY, which is the\ndecision-relevant half: a CLI catalogue comes from whoever RAN the tool, a\nclaims-file one travels WITH the repository.\n\nNO VERDICT CHANGED. Disclosure over restriction, per this item's own\nrecommendation (a): refusing user catalogues would close the case ADR-0016 §27\nbuilt the channel for, and the gap was never that users can extend the\ncatalogue — it was that doing so left no trace on the answer.\n\nBIGGEST BENEFICIARY: docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml, our own self-proof, declares\n6 taint-source + 6 taint-sink + 1 sanitizer catalogue via extra_catalogs and now\ndiscloses all 13 as repo-supplied. Legitimate — the safety zones ARE the design\n— but a reader of \"hypergumbo says this is safe\" is entitled to know the\ncriteria came from the subject.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES **NOT** CLOSE, stated so it is not inherited as done:\n - The TRUST question itself. A mislabelled overlay row still buys a\n   `confirmed`; it is now visible, not prevented. Option (b), ADR-0016's\n   unimplemented fourth verdict (\"confirmed with caveats\"), is the natural\n   consumer and was NOT built: consumers branch on `verdict`, so changing that\n   vocabulary pre-freeze is a different risk class from adding a field.\n - --taint-sanitizers remains an UNTESTED neighbour after three attempts that\n   produced no valid A/B (two put the sanitizer in the same function as the\n   source, a shape the tool discloses only ddg honours; the third had no\n   baseline finding). Filed separately rather than counted safe.\n - io-boundaries has the same stderr-only disclosure for the same overlays.\n   Out of scope here, which is about VERDICTS."  # e76e
